WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.050
Claimant: Hi, my car hit the rear of another car as I was approaching a traffic light. The front bumper and hood are dented, and the repair estimate is $2,800.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.100
Adjuster: Thanks—can you tell me what caused your car to hit the car ahead?

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.400
Claimant: I don’t know what caused it; I was driving, and the collision was accidental.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:44.850
Adjuster: Decision: covered. The claimant reports accidental front-end damage from hitting another vehicle, satisfying collision coverage with coverage prerequisites established by DEMO-DECL. No evidence supports the intentional-act exclusion, and the unknown cause does not create a material coverage gap under the supplied clauses. Next action: Approve collision coverage, verify the repair estimate, and apply the applicable limit and deductible.
